DECIDE `the assistants' supplement counts for` p IF
        p EQUALS `the hour value for extra work, of 17.5.2012`
    OR p EQUALS `leave, sick pay and their redemption, of 17.5.2012`
    OR p EQUALS `the determining salary for a budgetary pension, of 17.5.2012`
    OR p EQUALS `pension and training-fund contributions, of 17.5.2012`
    OR p EQUALS `severance pay, of 17.5.2012`
    OR p EQUALS `the 3.6% supplement of 31.1.01, of 17.5.2012`

#ASSERT NOT `the assistants' supplement counts for` `the minimum wage, of 17.5.2012`

-- The Sick Pay Law (imported), §§5–6: sick pay is the wage the employee
-- would have had working, and (5) pays the assistants' supplement in it. A
-- day of sick pay on the agreement's rule is the salary with the
-- supplement; checked as if §5 counted the supplement in the wage he would
-- have had (the strictest case: it is not one of §6(א)'s components by
-- name), it is the law's own measure. The redemption of unused sick days
-- it also counts for is no right the law gives. The floor is met.
GIVEN `the salary without the supplement` IS A NUMBER, `the supplement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `sick pay with the assistants' supplement` `the salary without the supplement` `the supplement` IS
    IF `the assistants' supplement counts for` `leave, sick pay and their redemption, of 17.5.2012`
    THEN `the salary without the supplement` PLUS `the supplement`
    ELSE `the salary without the supplement`

#ASSERT `sick pay with the assistants' supplement` 5000 500 AT LEAST `sick pay section 5 gives` 5500

-- The Annual Leave Law (imported), §10: holiday pay, and §13 its
-- redemption, are the regular wage, every payment for the regular hours
-- (§10(ג)); (5) counts the assistants' supplement for leave and for its
-- redemption, as §10(ג) counts a monthly supplement paid for the work. A
-- month of leave on the agreement's rule is the salary with the
-- supplement, the law's own measure. The floor is met.
GIVEN `the salary without the supplement` IS A NUMBER, `the supplement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `holiday pay with the assistants' supplement` `the salary without the supplement` `the supplement` IS
    IF `the assistants' supplement counts for` `leave, sick pay and their redemption, of 17.5.2012`
    THEN `the salary without the supplement` PLUS `the supplement`
    ELSE `the salary without the supplement`

`the assistants' supplement is in holiday pay as section 10 counts it` MEANS
        `section 10(ג) counts the payment in holiday pay` TRUE FALSE
    AND `holiday pay with the assistants' supplement` 5000 500
            AT LEAST `holiday pay section 10 gives one paid by the month` 5500
#ASSERT `the assistants' supplement is in holiday pay as section 10 counts it`

