-- (ה): from 1.1.2013 the מח"ר employees it covers are refunded their
-- professional association's dues, by the agreement to be signed for the
-- State's מח"ר employees under the 0.3% remainder of the agreement of
-- 14.1.2010 (outside the corpus) — the cost the recital adds.
@ref akn:art_9__para_e
`the מח"ר dues refund runs from` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2013

`the remainder §9(ה) of 17.5.2012 names` MEANS 0.3%

#ASSERT `the remainder §9(ה) of 17.5.2012 names` EQUALS `the cost the recital of 17.5.2012 adds, as the corpus reads it`

`why the dues refund is not here` MEANS
    `set elsewhere` "ההסכם הקיבוצי שייחתם לעובדי דירוג המח\"ר בשירות המדינה במסגרת יתרת עלות התוספות בשיעור 0.3% לפי ההסכם מיום 14.1.2010"

-- (ו): the agreement exhausts the parties' claims over or because of the
-- Ofek Hadash reform. (ז): earlier terms stand unless it amends or cancels
-- them expressly.
@ref akn:art_9__para_f akn:art_9__para_g
`the agreement of 17.5.2012 exhausts the claims over the Ofek Hadash reform` MEANS TRUE

GIVEN `it amends or cancels it expressly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an earlier term stays in force under 17.5.2012` `it amends or cancels it expressly` IF
    NOT `it amends or cancels it expressly`

-- (ח) industrial peace: (1) over the Ofek Hadash reform, no strike or
-- lockout, full or partial, nor other harm to the work, nationally or
-- locally — with no end set; (2) over the agreement's other matters, the
-- same until 31.12.2012.
@ref akn:art_9__para_h akn:art_9__para_h__subpara_1 akn:art_9__para_h__subpara_2
`no strike over the Ofek Hadash reform` MEANS
    PARTY `the New General Histadrut`
    SHANT `strike or harm the work over the Ofek Hadash reform`

`industrial peace over the other matters of 17.5.2012 ends on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2012

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `industrial peace of 17.5.2012 binds on the other matters on` d IF
    d `is on or before` `industrial peace over the other matters of 17.5.2012 ends on`

-- (ט): 0.075% is taken off the next framework's frame (after 31.12.2012)
-- for these employees.
@ref akn:art_9__para_i
`taken off the next frame for these employees` MEANS 0.075%

-- Against the Minimum Wage Law's floor (MMS-601). 5(ו), 6(ב)(4) and 7(ד) leave the
-- graded supplement, the assistants' supplement and the management
-- supplement out of the pay that counts toward the minimum wage, which
-- makes the top-up the law's or more (its §11). 4(ד) counts the Ma'of
-- supplement, and 9(ב) the supplement of §7 of 31.10.1999 from 1.10.2012:
-- each is a monthly supplement by grade, paid to every employee of the
-- grades for his work, which §3(ב)(3) counts too (convention
-- instruments.minimum-wage-fixed-supplement) — so the top-up is the law's.
-- That 4(ג) says the Ma'of supplement is no "fixed supplement" of the
-- non-unique agreement's §2.3 is that agreement's term, not the law's.
-- Checked on a month's figures as if §3 counted each (a fixed supplement for
-- the work), the strictest case for what is left out.
#ASSERT NOT `counting a component as the instrument does falls below the Minimum Wage Law` 5300 4800 (`component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law` `a fixed supplement paid for the work, under section 3(ב)(3)` 300) (`the graded supplement counts for` `the minimum wage, of 17.5.2012`)
#ASSERT NOT `counting a component as the instrument does falls below the Minimum Wage Law` 5300 4800 (`component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law` `a fixed supplement paid for the work, under section 3(ב)(3)` 300) (`the assistants' supplement counts for` `the minimum wage, of 17.5.2012`)
#ASSERT NOT `counting a component as the instrument does falls below the Minimum Wage Law` 5300 4800 (`component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law` `a fixed supplement paid for the work, under section 3(ב)(3)` 300) (`the management supplement counts for` `the minimum wage, of 17.5.2012`)
#ASSERT NOT `counting a component as the instrument does falls below the Minimum Wage Law` 5300 4800 (`component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law` `a fixed supplement paid for the work, under section 3(ב)(3)` 300) (`the Ma'of supplement counts for` `the minimum wage, of 17.5.2012`)
#ASSERT NOT `counting a component as the instrument does falls below the Minimum Wage Law` 5300 4800 (`component paid in the month under the Minimum Wage Law` `a fixed supplement paid for the work, under section 3(ב)(3)` 300) ((DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2012) `is on or after` `the 1999 supplement of grades 4–7 counts for the minimum wage from`)

§§ `10 ועדת מעקב`

-- (א): a committee of the Centre's or the three cities' representative and
-- the Histadrut's follows the agreement and decides its disputes
-- unanimously; (ב): failing agreement, a discussion with the parties and
-- the wages commissioner; (ג): failing a decision, either party may go to
-- the courts, or to another body if the committee and the parties agree.
@ref akn:art_10__para_a akn:art_10__para_b akn:art_10__para_c
`following the agreement of 17.5.2012` MEANS
    PARTY `the follow-up committee`
    MUST  `follow the agreement of 17.5.2012 and decide its disputes unanimously`
    LEST  (PARTY `the wages commissioner`
           MUST  `discuss an undecided dispute of 17.5.2012 with the wages commissioner`
           LEST  (PARTY `the employer`
                  MAY   `go to the courts over an undecided dispute of 17.5.2012`))

§§ `נספחים א' ו־ב' — טבלאות השכר המשולב`

-- The tables §6(ב)(2) attaches "for convenience" as annexes א' and ב': the
-- combined salary by seniority (rows 0 to 40) and grade, of the academics'
-- scale (מח"ר, engineers, practical engineers and technicians, and
-- journalists) and of the administrative scale ("דירוג אחיד"), as the
-- Treasury's wages division prints them. The page labels neither table
-- "א'" or "ב'"; they are written here in the page's order. Each is DATA,
-- cell for cell as the corpus publishes it (`a published table`,
-- tables-common.l4; tests/test_tables.py holds every cell by position). A
-- grade "N+" (with the stay supplement) is the column N.5, between the
-- grade and the next.
--
-- They print "בתוקף מ" 1.6.2005 and 1.6.2006, where §6(ב)(2) calls them
-- the tables "התקפות במועד חתימת הסכם זה": a table in force from a day
-- before the signing, and still in force on it. Nothing in the corpus
-- records a table that replaced them before 17.5.2012, so the two say the
-- same and nothing is read between them.

-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p1 akn:att_1__hc_1/p6 The Treasury's wages division heads each table; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p5 "נספח להסכם השכר", the page's caption between the two tables; no rule.

