-- in the administrative table every cell of grades 13+ to 16+ (seven
-- columns, seniority 0 to 40: 287 cells), in the academics' table grade 43
-- at seniority 30, whose agorot do not show. No rule here reads them.
`why the annexed tables' illegible cells of 17.5.2012 are not here` MEANS
    `the text is missing` "נספח השכר להסכם מיום 17.5.2012: בטבלת הדירוג האחיד דרגות 13+ עד 16+ בכל שנות הוותק (287 תאים), ובטבלת המח\"ר דרגה 43 בשנת ותק 30 — לא קריא"

-- Above each table: "תוספת ותק לשנה: עד 30: 1%, מ-31 עד 40: 0.75%" — a
-- year's seniority adds 1% to the 30th year and 0.75% from the 31st to the
-- 40th.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1/p3 akn:att_1__hc_1/p8
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the yearly seniority step of the annexed tables of 17.5.2012` `the year` IS
    IF `the year` AT MOST 30 THEN 1% ELSE 0.75%

GIVEN t IS A `published table`
GIVETH A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER AND NUMBER TO MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the seniority step of 17.5.2012 in` t IS
    GIVEN l, g YIELD
        CONSIDER `the published cell at` t (l MINUS 1) g
        WHEN JUST above THEN JUST (`to the agora` (above `increased by` (`the yearly seniority step of the annexed tables of 17.5.2012` l)))
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- A grade of §§4–5 as a column of the tables: the administrative scale's
-- number, or the academics' (number + 30), "+" the half column beside it.
GIVEN g IS A `grade of 17.5.2012`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the administrative column of` g IS
    g's `the grade's number, of 17.5.2012` PLUS (IF g's `with the stay supplement, of 17.5.2012` THEN 0.5 ELSE 0)

GIVEN g IS A `grade of 17.5.2012`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the academics' column of` g IS
    `the administrative column of` g PLUS 30

-- The combined salary the annexed tables print for a grade and a year of
-- seniority (what §6's 10% and §7's management supplement are computed on,
-- as the tables stood at the signing; §6(ב)(2) sends a later month to the
-- commissioner's circulars).
GIVEN g IS A `grade of 17.5.2012`, seniority IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the annexed administrative combined salary of 17.5.2012 for` g seniority IS
    `the published cell at` `the annexed administrative scale table of 17.5.2012` seniority (`the administrative column of` g)

GIVEN g IS A `grade of 17.5.2012`, seniority IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the annexed academics' combined salary of 17.5.2012 for` g seniority IS
    `the published cell at` `the annexed academics' scale table of 17.5.2012` seniority (`the academics' column of` g)

§§ `בדיקת הנספחים`

-- (1) The rows: seniority 0 to 40 in both; the grades 2 to 13 (the
-- administrative scale's legible columns) and 34 to 46+.
#ASSERT `the published labels of` `the annexed academics' scale table of 17.5.2012` EQUALS range 0 40
#ASSERT `the published labels of` `the annexed administrative scale table of 17.5.2012` EQUALS range 0 40
#ASSERT `the published cell count of` `the annexed administrative scale table of 17.5.2012` EQUALS 41 TIMES 29 MINUS 287
#ASSERT `the published cell count of` `the annexed academics' scale table of 17.5.2012` EQUALS 41 TIMES 26 MINUS 1

-- (2) The seniority step the tables print above them, to the agora: every
-- cell with one above it is that cell raised by the year's step, or an
-- agora off it (the tables round each year's cell, and the next year is
-- computed on the unrounded figure).
`the step checks of the annexed academics' table of 17.5.2012` MEANS
    `the published cells beside` (`the seniority step of 17.5.2012 in` `the annexed academics' scale table of 17.5.2012`) `in` `the annexed academics' scale table of 17.5.2012`

`the step checks of the annexed administrative table of 17.5.2012` MEANS
    `the published cells beside` (`the seniority step of 17.5.2012 in` `the annexed administrative scale table of 17.5.2012`) `in` `the annexed administrative scale table of 17.5.2012`

#ASSERT count `the step checks of the annexed academics' table of 17.5.2012` EQUALS 1038
#ASSERT `the published worst miss in` `the step checks of the annexed academics' table of 17.5.2012` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT count `the step checks of the annexed administrative table of 17.5.2012` EQUALS 880
#ASSERT `the published worst miss in` `the step checks of the annexed administrative table of 17.5.2012` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the published table rises along its grades and down its rows` `the annexed academics' scale table of 17.5.2012`
#ASSERT `the published table rises along its grades and down its rows` `the annexed administrative scale table of 17.5.2012`

-- (3) Every grade §4 and §5 price, 4 to 10+ and 34 to 40+, is a column of
-- the tables, so the reading "a מח"ר grade is its number less 30" names a
-- printed grade on both scales.
`the grades §§4–5 of 17.5.2012 price` MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN n YIELD LIST `grade of 17.5.2012` n FALSE, `grade of 17.5.2012` n TRUE) (range 4 10))

#ASSERT all (GIVEN g YIELD elem (`the administrative column of` g) (`the published grades of` `the annexed administrative scale table of 17.5.2012`)) `the grades §§4–5 of 17.5.2012 price`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN g YIELD elem (`the academics' column of` g) (`the published grades of` `the annexed academics' scale table of 17.5.2012`)) `the grades §§4–5 of 17.5.2012 price`

-- (4) §4(ו)'s example takes "the larger" of 22% of the combined salary and
-- §2.2's 1,400 to be 1,400 for an employee of grade 8, naming no
-- seniority: on the annexed tables 22% of every grade-8 cell (and of every
-- grade-38 cell) is below 1,400, so the example holds at any seniority.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN l YIELD
                 CONSIDER `the annexed administrative combined salary of 17.5.2012 for` (`grade of 17.5.2012` 8 FALSE) l
                 WHEN JUST c THEN max (22% TIMES c) `§2.2's amount as the Ma'of agreement of 2009 updated it` EQUALS 1400
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)
            (range 0 40)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN l YIELD
                 CONSIDER `the annexed academics' combined salary of 17.5.2012 for` (`grade of 17.5.2012` 8 FALSE) l
                 WHEN JUST c THEN max (22% TIMES c) `§2.2's amount as the Ma'of agreement of 2009 updated it` EQUALS 1400
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)
            (range 0 40)

-- The tables at work: a grade of §§4–5 read as a column of each table,
-- at seniority 0.
#ASSERT `the annexed administrative combined salary of 17.5.2012 for` (`grade of 17.5.2012` 7 FALSE) 0 EQUALS JUST 2344.71
#ASSERT `the annexed academics' combined salary of 17.5.2012 for` (`grade of 17.5.2012` 4 FALSE) 0 EQUALS JUST 2007.26
